MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`cotty agent <join-url>` joins a session as an ordinary guest backed by a
model: Anthropic's Messages API (default claude-opus-5-5) or any
OpenAI-compatible chat endpoint (OpenAI, OpenRouter, Ollama, ...). It
keeps a plain-text view of the shared screen and answers questions asked
from inside the hosted shell with `cotty ask`; the answer is printed by
`cotty ask` itself, so every participant sees it and recordings keep it.

Like any guest it starts view-only and proposes commands instead of
running them. After `cotty ctl allow agent` it types one command line per
step, reads the result, and reports back; deny and kick work as for
people, and the audit trail attributes its keystrokes, questions (ask)
and answers (say).

Protocol: two new frames, ask (host to guests) and say (guest to host,
fanned out to everyone), sealed like output in end-to-end encrypted
sessions. Relays forward them and attribute say by guest name. Chat is
not gated by write permission, so it is rate limited per sender.

Also fixes `cotty ctl list` through a relay running every guest onto one
line: the control result was sanitized with SanitizeText, which strips
newlines. SanitizeLines keeps them and still strips other control
characters.

